  "Date": "2026-11-09T16:56:29Z",
  "Message": "Choose optional features per site; ship inbound email with Haraka\n\nThe status page grayed out a fixed list of components on every Helm\ninstall, chosen when the chart was first validated rather than per site.\nOptional components are now chart switches, and the grayed-out list is\nderived from them, so a gray card means \"this site doesn't run it\".\n\n- inboundMail (on by default): Haraka runs in the cluster as non-root\n  on 2525; a Traefik IngressRouteTCP on the `smtp` entrypoint publishes\n  port 25. STARTTLS uses the ingress certificate. Recipients are still\n  checked with Orbital at RCPT time. The Haraka image is built and\n  scanned with the release.\n- INBOUND_MAIL_DOMAIN is now always set (inbound.<domain> by default).\n  Charts never set it before, so reply-to addresses on Kubernetes used\n  the dev-only inbound.orbital.test.\n- ollama (off by default): Ollama as a StatefulSet with a model volume;\n  OLLAMA_URL points at it while enabled.\n- health.probes / HEALTH_PROBES say where each card's component lives,\n  and the chart fills it for what it deploys.\n- The Mail card now judges the mailer in use (log, SMTP relay, or an\n  API mailer and its key). The TLS card reads the certificate actually\n  served when Orbital doesn't manage one, which is the case on\n  Kubernetes, where cert-manager holds it.\n- ORBITAL_MANAGED_SETTINGS marks Platform Settings fields the\n  deployment sets (inbound domain and token): shown read-only, and a\n  saved value is ignored, so the UI can't drift from Haraka or the MX\n  record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
  "Tags": [],
  "Fingerprint": "b8668d4d4b76ea451615bc5baf5028ac7f3d3676:config/health.php:generic-api-key:34"
 },
